    dict(key='20-act-5-figure', kind='figure', title='Tenants, an old event, a delete, and Grafana',
         body='tenants',
         narration="Fifth demo: the bill. [[slnc 400]] At the top left, another tenant, the shop, asks for the bank's lines. [[slnc 300]] It gets none: tenants keep the data apart. [[slnc 600]] At the top right, Grafana. [[slnc 300]] Each data source sends one tenant header. [[slnc 300]] Through the bank's data source, Grafana finds the same six failures as Loki. [[slnc 300]] Through the shop's, nothing. [[slnc 300]] So whoever may use the bank's data source can read the bank's logs. [[slnc 600]] In the middle, an event stamped ten days ago. [[slnc 300]] The limit is one hundred sixty eight hours, which is seven days, so it is refused. [[slnc 300]] And asking Loki to delete lines gets four oh four: the route is not there. [[slnc 600]] At the bottom, what stays the team's job."),
    dict(key='21-act-5-1', kind='console', title='Act Five — The bill',
         body='FIVE. The bill.\n  ANOTHER TENANT, shop, ASKS FOR {app="bank"}:\n    lines   0 (the tenant bank sees 12)\n    labels  none\n  AN EVENT STAMPED TEN DAYS AGO:\n    limit   reject_old_samples_max_age 168h = 168 / 24 = 7 days\n    event   10 days old > 7 days\n    answer  400 timestamp too old  <- REFUSED\n  ASKING LOKI TO DELETE THE BANK\'S LINES:\n    answer  404: no such route until deletion is configured\n    and no route at all changes a line once it is stored',
         narration="Here is the output. [[slnc 300]] The shop tenant asks for the bank's lines and gets zero; the bank itself sees twelve. [[slnc 400]] An event ten days old: the limit is one hundred sixty eight hours, divided by twenty four, seven days. [[slnc 300]] Ten is more than seven, so it is refused with four hundred. [[slnc 400]] A delete request gets four oh four."),
